<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"  xml:id="ch_counting">
  <title>Listing and Counting</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Since listing and counting are at the heart of discrete mathematics,
      many answers in this chapter are counting functions into <m>\nats</m>.
      We begin our journey there in 
      <xref ref="sec_listing"></xref>
       <m>\seclisting</m>,
      <xref ref="sec_counting_steps_cases"></xref>
      <m>\subsetsdigits</m>,
      <xref ref="sec_counting_subsets"></xref> 
      <m>\substrings</m>,
      and <xref ref="sec_bit_strings"></xref> 
      <m>\subintalgebra</m>,.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include  href="sec_listing.ptx"/>
  
  <xi:include  href="sec_counting_steps_cases.ptx"/>
  <xi:include  href="sec_counting_subsets.ptx"/>
  <xi:include  href="sec_bit_strings.ptx"/>
  
</chapter>